<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>LIFE TABLES (Single Decrement Tables)_q4</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the Australian Males Life Table \((1960-62)-\text{A}^{\text{M}61}\) given below to answer the question that follows.</p>
<p><strong style="color: blue;">
 <a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1HLhNdPh1r0467c_FfyHkov1UPUZk1ZE1">Download Australian Males Life Table Data </a>
</strong></p>
<p>Using the life tables for Australian Males, estimate the following measures.</p>
<p>What is the expected age at death assuming \(A^{m61}\) mortality of three groups of persons now aged \({@age_index1@}\), \({@age_index2@}\) and \({@age_index3@}\) respectively.</p>
<p><b>Note:</b> Give your answers correct to \(2\) decimal places.</p>
<p>\((a)\,\) Persons now aged \({@age_index1@}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\((b)\,\) Persons now aged \({@age_index2@}=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\((c)\,\) Persons now aged \({@age_index3@}=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Persons now aged \({@age_index1@}\) on the average are expected to live further \(e^0{@age_index1@}\) years and hence their average age at death is;</p>
<p>\((a). \, {@age_index1@} + \frac{T_{{@age_index1@}}}{l_{{@age_index1@}}}={@age_index1@}+\frac{{@T_num_1@}}{{@l_num_1@}}={@age_index1@}+{@decimalplaces((T_num_1/l_num_1),2)@}={@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>\((b). \, {@age_index2@} + \frac{T_{{@age_index2@}}}{l_{{@age_index2@}}}={@age_index2@}+\frac{{@T_num_2@}}{{@l_num_2@}}={@age_index2@}+{@decimalplaces((T_num_2/l_num_2),2)@}={@ta2@}\)</p>
<p>\((c). \, {@age_index3@} + \frac{T_{{@age_index3@}}}{l_{{@age_index3@}}}={@age_index3@}+\frac{{@T_num_3@}}{{@l_num_3@}}={@age_index3@}+{@decimalplaces((T_num_3/l_num_3),2)@}={@ta3@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
